---
import PageSite from "@layouts/PageSite.astro";
import PageHead from "@components/redesign/PageHead.astro";
---

<PageSite title="FLL Curriculum" description="StuyPulse's FIRST LEGO League curriculum for new teams and mentors, and our history mentoring FLL." fullBleed>
  <PageHead title="FLL Curriculum" intro="Our FIRST LEGO League curriculum gives new teams and their mentors a solid start, from robot basics to the research project.">
    <a slot="before" class="back" href="/resources/tutorials">Tutorials</a>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="pill pill-white" href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1HHpAj9i55wv1z8ngOnp6s4ErxipuHmxV?usp=sharing">Open the curriculum</a>
    </div>
  </PageHead>

  <div class="band prose">
    <h2>StuyPulse and FLL</h2>
    <p>
      It began in the spring of 2001, when Team 694 gave a presentation to teachers about starting a robotics curriculum.
      Since then we've helped several schools join FLL, and mentored teams, especially I.S. 89 across the street, which
      we've mentored every year since 2002.
    </p>
    <p>
      In December 2005 we hosted the first Manhattan Borough FLL Tournament at our school, and later brought it up to the
      standards of an official FIRST event. We've also sent volunteers to referee and queue teams at the NYC FLL tournament
      at Riverbank State Park and at the Queens FLL Qualifier.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since 2019 we've helped FLL teams in Puerto Rico with programming and their project presentations: the ASJ
      Robotigers, Knight Hackers, The LEGO Builders and The Robogens. In 2024 we wrote our own FLL curriculum, which is
      linked above.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageSite>

